{"aliases": ["email_person"], "categories": ["common", "internet", "pii"], "classification": "identifier", "doc": "Address of an electronic mailbox in the form local-part@domain, defined in section 3.4.1 of RFC 5322. The local part names the mailbox, and the domain says which mail server accepts messages for it. The standard grammar also allows quoted local parts, comments and IP address literals, and RFC 6531 allows non-ASCII characters; the regexp covers the common form: letters, digits and . _ % + - in the local part and a dotted domain name.", "examples": [{"description": "Plain address", "valid": true, "value": "user@example.com"}, {"description": "Dots, a plus tag and a subdomain", "valid": true, "value": "first.last+tag@mail.example.org"}, {"description": "No domain", "valid": false, "value": "user@"}, {"description": "No @", "valid": false, "value": "user.example.com"}], "id": "email", "is_pii": true, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Email_address"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "https://schema.org/email"}, {"type": "wikidata", "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Property:P968"}, {"type": "doc", "url": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5322.html#section-3.4.1"}], "mappings": {"autotype": "email", "cdm": "means.identity.service.email", "d3m": "http://schema.org/email", "dpv": "pd:EmailAddress", "fibo": "FND/Places/VirtualPlaces/ElectronicMailAddress", "fta": "EMAIL", "google_dlp": "EMAIL_ADDRESS", "presidio": "EMAIL_ADDRESS", "schema_org": "email", "wikidata": "P968"}, "name": "Email address", "regexp": "^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9-]{1,62}$", "status": "stable", "translations": {"ru": {"doc": "Адрес почтового ящика в форме локальная_часть@домен (RFC 5322).", "name": "Адрес электронной почты"}}, "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/email", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/email.json"}}
{"categories": ["finances"], "checksum": "iban_mod97", "children": ["be_iban", "cz_iban", "de_iban", "es_iban", "kz_iban", "me_iban", "nl_iban", "no_iban"], "classification": "identifier", "doc": "The International Bank Account Number (IBAN) is an internationally agreed system of identifying bank accounts across national borders to facilitate the communication and processing of cross border transactions with a reduced risk of transcription errors. An IBAN uniquely identifies the account of a customer at a financial institution.", "examples": [{"description": "Documentation example, electronic format", "valid": true, "value": "GB82WEST12345698765432"}, {"description": "The same IBAN in print format", "valid": true, "value": "GB82 WEST 1234 5698 7654 32"}, {"description": "German documentation example", "valid": true, "value": "DE89370400440532013000"}, {"description": "Last digit changed: fails the mod-97 check", "valid": false, "value": "GB82WEST12345698765433"}], "id": "iban", "is_pii": false, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Bank_Account_Number"}], "mappings": {"autotype": "iban", "dpv": "pd:BankAccount", "fibo": "FBC/ProductsAndServices/ClientsAndAccounts/InternationalBankAccountIdentifier", "fta": "CHECKDIGIT.IBAN", "google_dlp": "IBAN_CODE", "gs1_ai": "8007", "presidio": "IBAN_CODE", "purview": "International banking account number (IBAN)", "stdnum": "iban"}, "name": "International Bank Account Number", "regexp": "^[A-Z]{2}\\d{2}(?: ?[A-Z0-9]){11,30}$", "status": "stable", "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/iban", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/iban.json"}}
{"aliases": ["ssn"], "categories": ["pii", "persons"], "classification": "identifier", "country": ["US"], "doc": "In the United States, a Social Security number (SSN) is a nine-digit number issued to U.S. citizens, permanent residents, and temporary (working) residents under section 205(c)(2) of the Social Security Act, codified as 42 U.S.C. § 405(c)(2)", "id": "usssn", "is_pii": true, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["en"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_Security_number"}], "mappings": {"autotype": ["ssn", "ssn - new"], "dpv": "pd:OfficialID", "fhir": "http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/us-ssn", "fta": "SSN", "google_dlp": "US_SOCIAL_SECURITY_NUMBER", "presidio": "US_SSN", "purview": "U.S. social security number (SSN)", "stdnum": "us.ssn"}, "name": "US Social Security Number", "regexp": "([0-9]{3})[- .]([0-9]{2})[- .]([0-9]{4})", "status": "stable", "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/usssn", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/usssn.json"}}
{"aliases": ["guid"], "categories": ["identifiers"], "children": ["musicbrainz_id", "uuid_v1", "uuid_v4", "uuid_v7"], "classification": "identifier", "doc": "128-bit identifier that systems generate without a central registry, defined by RFC 9562 (2024), which replaced RFC 4122. Microsoft calls it a GUID. The text form is 32 hexadecimal digits in five groups of 8, 4, 4, 4 and 12 separated by hyphens, in any letter case. The first digit of the third group is the version (1 to 8, see uuid_v1, uuid_v4 and uuid_v7), and the first digit of the fourth group is 8, 9, a or b for the RFC 9562 variant. The Nil UUID (all zeros) and the Max UUID (all f) are special values. Microsoft tools and the Windows registry write GUIDs in curly braces, a form the regexp also accepts. The regexp does not accept the 32 digits without hyphens, which look like an MD5 hash, or the urn:uuid form (uuid_urn).", "examples": [{"description": "Example string UUID of RFC 9562 (Figure 1)", "valid": true, "value": "f81d4fae-7dec-11d0-a765-00a0c91e6bf6"}, {"description": "UUIDv4 test vector of RFC 9562 (Appendix A.3)", "valid": true, "value": "919108f7-52d1-4320-9bac-f847db4148a8"}, {"description": "Name-based UUIDv3 from the Python uuid module documentation", "valid": true, "value": "6fa459ea-ee8a-3ca4-894e-db77e160355e"}, {"description": "UUIDv1 test vector of RFC 9562 in the braced GUID form of Microsoft tools", "valid": true, "value": "{C232AB00-9414-11EC-B3C8-9F6BDECED846}"}, {"description": "32 hexadecimal digits without hyphens", "valid": false, "value": "f81d4fae7dec11d0a76500a0c91e6bf6"}, {"description": "URN form, see uuid_urn", "valid": false, "value": "urn:uuid:f81d4fae-7dec-11d0-a765-00a0c91e6bf6"}, {"description": "Unbalanced brace", "valid": false, "value": "{f81d4fae-7dec-11d0-a765-00a0c91e6bf6"}], "id": "uuid", "is_pii": false, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universally_unique_identifier"}, {"type": "wikidata", "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q195284"}, {"type": "doc", "url": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562"}], "mappings": {"autotype": "guid", "cdm": "is.dataFormat.guid", "fta": "GUID", "presidio": "UUID"}, "name": "Universally unique identifier (UUID)", "patterns": ["uuid_urn"], "regexp": "^(?:[0-9A-Fa-f]{8}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{12}|\\{[0-9A-Fa-f]{8}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{12}\\})$", "status": "stable", "translations": {"ru": {"doc": "128-битный идентификатор по RFC 9562, который системы создают без центрального реестра. В Microsoft его называют GUID. Записывается как 32 шестнадцатеричные цифры в пяти группах (8-4-4-4-12) через дефис; первая цифра третьей группы указывает версию.", "name": "Универсальный уникальный идентификатор (UUID)"}}, "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/uuid", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/uuid.json"}}
{"categories": ["common"], "classification": "categorical", "doc": "In computer science, the Boolean data type is a data type that has one of two possible values (usually denoted true and false) which is intended to represent the two truth values of logic and Boolean algebra.", "id": "boolean", "is_pii": false, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boolean_data_type"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "https://schema.org/Boolean"}], "mappings": {"d3m": "http://schema.org/Boolean"}, "name": "Boolean", "status": "stable", "translations": {"ru": {"doc": "Логи́ческий тип да́нных, или булев тип, или булевый тип (от англ. Boolean или logical data type) — примитивный тип данных в информатике, принимающий два возможных значения, иногда называемых истиной (true) и ложью (false).", "name": "Логический тип"}}, "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/boolean", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/boolean.json"}}
{"categories": ["pii", "common", "telecom"], "children": ["msisdn"], "doc": "Telephone number in standard format (RFC3966), without 'tel:' prefix", "examples": [{"description": "White House", "valid": true, "value": "+1-202-456-1414"}, {"description": "International Civil Aviation Organization", "valid": true, "value": "+1-514-954-8219"}], "id": "phone", "is_pii": true, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikidata", "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Property:P1329"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "https://schema.org/telephone"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "https://schema.org/faxNumber"}, {"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telephone_number"}], "mappings": {"autotype": "phone-3", "cdm": "means.identity.service.phone", "dpv": "pd:TelephoneNumber", "fibo": "FND/Places/VirtualPlaces/TelephoneNumber", "fta": "TELEPHONE", "google_dlp": "PHONE_NUMBER", "presidio": "PHONE_NUMBER", "schema_org": "telephone", "wikidata": "P1329"}, "name": "Phone number", "patterns": ["nanpphone", "phone_e164", "tel_uri"], "regexp": "(?=.*\\d)(?:(?:(?:\\+|00|011)[\\.\\/\\-\\ \\t]*([17]|2(?:[07]|[1-689]\\d)|3(?:[0-4679]|[578]\\d)|4(?:[013-9]|2\\d)|5(?:[1-8]|[09]\\d)|6(?:[0-6]|[789]\\d)|8(?:[1246]|[035789]\\d)|9(?:[0-58]|[679]\\d))[\\.\\/\\-\\ \\t]*|([17])[\\.\\/\\-\\ ])?(?:\\((\\d{1,6})\\)[\\.\\/\\-\\ \\t]*)?(?:(\\d{1,6})[\\.\\/\\-\\ ])?(?:(\\d{1,6})[\\.\\/\\-\\ ])?(?:(\\d{1,6})[\\.\\/\\-\\ ])?(?:(\\d{1,6})[\\.\\/\\-\\ ])?(\\d{0,10}?)(\\d{1,4})(?:[\\.\\/\\-;\\ \\t]*e?xt?[\\.\\/\\-=\\ \\t]*(\\d{1,14}))?)?", "status": "stable", "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/phone", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/phone.json"}}
{"categories": ["datetime"], "children": ["birthday", "deathday"], "doc": "Calendar date. The regexp covers the ISO 8601 extended form YYYY-MM-DD; other notations, such as DD.MM.YYYY, are patterns of this datatype.", "examples": [{"description": "ISO 8601 date", "valid": true, "value": "2025-05-15"}, {"description": "Date of a document in the register of cultural heritage objects", "valid": true, "value": "1993-12-30"}, {"description": "There is no month 13", "valid": false, "value": "2025-13-01"}, {"description": "Day-first notation, the pattern date_dmy", "valid": false, "value": "15.05.2025"}], "id": "date", "is_pii": false, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_and_time_notation"}, {"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "https://schema.org/Date"}], "mappings": {"autotype": ["date-chinese", "date-d", "date-hijri", "date1", "date10", "date2", "date3", "date4"], "cdm": "means.measurement.date", "presidio": "DATE_TIME", "qddate": "dt:date:date_9"}, "name": "Date", "patterns": ["date_bulgarian", "date_cjk", "date_czech", "date_dmy", "date_dmy_compact", "date_dmy_dash", "date_dmy_dash_yy", "date_dmy_dot_yy", "date_dmy_slash", "date_dmy_slash_yy", "date_dutch", "date_english", "date_french", "date_german", "date_italian", "date_korean", "date_mdy_slash", "date_mdy_slash_yy", "date_polish", "date_portuguese", "date_romanian", "date_russian", "date_slovak", "date_spanish", "date_turkish", "date_ukrainian", "date_ymd_compact", "date_ymd_dot", "date_ymd_slash"], "regexp": "^\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$", "status": "stable", "translations": {"ru": {"doc": "Календарная дата. Регулярное выражение описывает форму ISO 8601 ГГГГ-ММ-ДД; другие нотации, например ДД.ММ.ГГГГ, описаны шаблонами этого типа.", "name": "Дата"}}, "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/date", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/date.json"}}
{"categories": ["datetime"], "doc": "Date and time of day. The regexp covers the ISO 8601 extended form YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm[:ss[.fff]] with an optional time zone (Z or an offset), and the RFC 3339 variant with a space instead of T. Some data sets store plain dates as timestamps at midnight local time, for example 2021-05-24T21:00:00.000Z for 25 May 2021 in Moscow.", "examples": [{"description": "UTC timestamp with milliseconds", "valid": true, "value": "2024-08-30T12:00:00.000Z"}, {"valid": true, "value": "2018-10-10T12:58:52Z"}, {"description": "Space separator, as allowed by RFC 3339", "valid": true, "value": "2024-11-29 12:00:00"}, {"description": "Local time with an offset", "valid": true, "value": "2019-07-19T09:00:00+03:00"}, {"description": "A date without a time is the datatype date", "valid": false, "value": "2024-08-30"}], "id": "datetime", "is_pii": false, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_and_time_notation"}, {"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "https://schema.org/DateTime"}], "mappings": {"autotype": ["date-R", "date-chinese2", "date-f", "date-g", "date-german", "date-mixed", "date-o", "date-s", "date-spanish", "date-u", "date5", "date6", "date7", "date8", "date9"], "d3m": "http://schema.org/DateTime"}, "name": "Date and time", "regexp": "^\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])[T ](?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d(?::[0-5]\\d(?:[.,]\\d+)?)?(?:Z|[+-](?:[01]\\d|2[0-3])(?::?[0-5]\\d)?)?$", "status": "stable", "translations": {"ru": {"doc": "Дата и время суток. Регулярное выражение описывает форму ISO 8601 ГГГГ-ММ-ДДTчч:мм[:сс[.fff]] с необязательным часовым поясом (Z или смещение) и вариант RFC 3339 с пробелом вместо T.", "name": "Дата и время"}}, "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/datetime", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/datetime.json"}}
{"categories": ["datetime"], "doc": "Calendar date written as a two-digit day, a two-digit month and a four-digit year separated by dots, such as 31.12.2022. This day-first notation is the usual one in Russia, Germany and many other countries.", "examples": [{"valid": true, "value": "31.12.2022"}, {"description": "Start date of archaeological works in the open data of the Russian Ministry of Culture", "valid": true, "value": "01.10.2021"}, {"description": "Year-first notation", "valid": false, "value": "2022.12.31"}, {"description": "There is no day 32", "valid": false, "value": "32.01.2022"}], "id": "date_dmy", "is_pii": false, "kind": "pattern", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_format_by_country"}, {"type": "other", "url": "https://github.com/ivbeg/qddate/blob/v1.1.0/qddate/patterns/base.py"}], "mappings": {"qddate": "dt:date:date_2"}, "name": "Date in DD.MM.YYYY notation", "regexp": "^(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])\\.(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])\\.\\d{4}$", "semantic_type": "date", "status": "draft", "translations": {"ru": {"name": "Дата в формате ДД.ММ.ГГГГ"}}, "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/date_dmy", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/date_dmy.json"}}
{"categories": ["pii", "persons"], "classification": "identifier", "country": ["CA"], "doc": "Social insurance number (SIN) is a number issued in Canada to administer various government programs.", "id": "casin", "is_pii": true, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["en"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_insurance_number"}], "mappings": {"dpv": "pd:OfficialID", "fta": "IDENTITY.SIN_CA", "google_dlp": "CANADA_SOCIAL_INSURANCE_NUMBER", "presidio": "CA_SIN", "purview": "Canada social insurance number", "stdnum": "ca.sin"}, "name": "Canada social insurance number (SIN)", "regexp": "(\\d{3}-\\d{3}-\\d{3})|(\\d{9})", "status": "stable", "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/casin", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/casin.json"}}
{"categories": ["geo", "common"], "classification": "identifier", "doc": "In geography, latitude is a geographic coordinate that specifies the north–south position of a point on the Earths surface. Latitude is an angle (defined below) which ranges from 0° at the Equator to 90° (North or South) at the poles.", "id": "latitude", "is_pii": false, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latitude"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "http://schema.org/latitude"}], "mappings": {"cdm": "means.location.latitude", "d3m": "http://schema.org/latitude", "fta": ["COORDINATE.LATITUDE_DECIMAL", "COORDINATE.LATITUDE_DMS"], "schema_org": "latitude"}, "name": "latitude", "status": "stable", "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/latitude", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/latitude.json"}}
{"categories": ["geo", "common"], "doc": "Longitude is a geographic coordinate that specifies the east–west position of a point on the Earths surface, or the surface of a celestial body. It is an angular measurement, usually expressed in degrees and denoted by the Greek letter lambda (λ)", "id": "longitude", "is_pii": false, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longitude"}, {"type": "schema.org", "url": "http://schema.org/longitude"}], "mappings": {"cdm": "means.location.longitude", "d3m": "http://schema.org/longitude", "fta": ["COORDINATE.LONGITUDE_DECIMAL", "COORDINATE.LONGITUDE_DMS"], "schema_org": "longitude"}, "name": "Longitude", "status": "stable", "urls": {"html": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/datatype/longitude", "json": "https://registry.apicrafter.io/api/v1/datatypes/longitude.json"}}
{"aliases": ["eui48"], "categories": ["internet", "identifiers", "pii"], "classification": "identifier", "doc": "48-bit hardware address (EUI-48) of a network interface in Ethernet, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and other IEEE 802 networks, used to deliver frames within one network segment. The first three octets usually hold the OUI of the manufacturer; the second-lowest bit of the first octet marks a locally administered address, such as the random addresses that phones use on Wi-Fi. It is written as six pairs of hexadecimal digits separated by hyphens (IEEE style) or colons, or as three groups of four digits separated by dots (Cisco style). RFC 9542 reserves 00-00-5E-00-53-00 to 00-00-5E-00-53-FF for documentation. 64-bit identifiers are described by eui64.", "examples": [{"description": "Documentation address of RFC 9542, IEEE notation", "valid": true, "value": "00-00-5E-00-53-01"}, {"description": "Documentation address of RFC 9542 with colons", "valid": true, "value": "00:00:5e:00:53:af"}, {"description": "Documentation address of RFC 9542 in dotted notation", "valid": true, "value": "0000.5e00.5301"}, {"description": "Mixed separators", "valid": false, "value": "00:00:5E-00-53:01"}, {"description": "Five octets", "valid": false, "value": "00-00-5E-00-53"}, {"description": "Eight octets: an EUI-64 identifier", "valid": false, "value": "00-00-5E-EF-10-00-00-01"}], "id": "mac_address", "is_pii": true, "kind": "datatype", "langs": ["common"], "links": [{"type": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MAC_address"}, {"type": "doc", "url": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9542"}, {"type": "doc", "url": "https://standards.ieee.org/wp-content/uploads/import/documents/tutorials/eui.pdf"}], "mappings": {"autotype": "mac", "dpv": "pd:MACAddress", "fhir": "http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/eui-48/ethernet", "fta": "MACADDRESS", "google_dlp": "MAC_ADDRESS", "presidio": "MAC_ADDRESS", "stdnum": "mac"}, "name": "MAC address (Media Access Control)", "regexp": "^(?:[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}(?:-[0